# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a tag stop delivered at an internal safepoint inside a `|`-chain
#         unwinds the current strand through the cleanup stack, executing
#         finally bodies and popping TAG_SCOPE entries in order (row 12 §5.3
#         — safepoint delivery of pending UEXEC_TAG_STOP unwind).
#
# blocked: requires string concat (T46 dropped); log = log + "a" pattern blocked
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason: verifying tag.stop() delivered at an internal pipe safepoint requires
# calling t.stop() from within the tag scope body.  Method call syntax
# (obj.method()) requires the M4 object model (prototype chain dispatch).
# At M3, OP_PUSH_TAG/OP_POP_TAG are emitted and the unwind walker handles
# UEXEC_TAG_STOP absorption for TAG_SCOPE frames; the gap is the urbiscript
# surface for invoking the stop.  Synchronous single-strand tag stop with
# finally is substantively tested in tests/chk/control_transfer/ and the
# C-API-driven cross_strand_cancel.chk fixture.
#
# When M4 lands (Tag.stop() method), implement this by:
#   var log = ""
#   var t = Tag.new
#   t: {
#     try { log = log + "a" | t.stop() | log = log + "c" }
#     finally { log = log + "F" }
#   }
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "aF"
